From: Etienne Carriere <etienne.carriere@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 19 Dec 2023 10:48:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 0283/1695] drivers: gic: fix local variables definition

Fix gic_it_set_cpu_mask() local variables definition.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git cd8b71f865f820fc23134746e2f0cc74bdc048a2 drivers: gic: fix local variables definition]
Change-Id: Ia6ca5cc606e1b68abe84315ee37c955cf0f8343d
Signed-off-by: Etienne Carriere <etienne.carriere@foss.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/gic.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/gic.c b/core/drivers/gic.c
index 9d35922dc..f56e1650f 100644
--- a/core/drivers/gic.c
+++ b/core/drivers/gic.c
@@ -392,7 +392,8 @@ static void gic_it_set_cpu_mask(struct gic_data *gd, size_t it,
 {
 	size_t idx __maybe_unused = it / NUM_INTS_PER_REG;
 	uint32_t mask __maybe_unused = 1 << (it % NUM_INTS_PER_REG);
-	uint32_t target, target_shift;
+	uint32_t target = 0;
+	uint32_t target_shift = 0;
 	vaddr_t itargetsr = gd->gicd_base +
 			    GICD_ITARGETSR(it / NUM_TARGETS_PER_REG);
 
